### tracking-service local exercise file
# REST Client (VS Code) — runs the two REST read endpoints of the service.
# Boot the server first: `npm run dev` (loads .env via tsx --env-file).
#
# NOTE on paths: the service mounts the reads under `/v1/tracking`, so the path
# is the same whether you hit tracking-service DIRECTLY (this file,
# `:3005/v1/tracking/...`) or via the gateway (`/v1/tracking/...`) — the gateway
# forwards `/v1` pass-through (it does not add or strip it). The WebSocket
# (`/v1/tracking/socket.io/`) is exercised separately — see
# docs/manual-testing-guide.md + the simulate-driver.ts script; a REST Client
# file can't drive a Socket.IO connection.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THE BIG PICTURE: there is NO HTTP endpoint that starts tracking. An order
# becomes trackable when the service CONSUMES `order.created` (→ customerId)
# and `dispatch.driver.assigned` (→ driverId) into the `tracking_orders`
# projection, and points appear only once a driver streams `location:update`
# over the WebSocket. So to get a non-empty /latest or /route you FIRST drive
# the projection + a point in (see the manual-testing-guide), THEN read here.
#
# PREREQUISITES:
#
#   1. Mongo + Redis + RabbitMQ. `docker compose up -d` brings up the dev
#      Mongo (:27018) + Redis (:6380). RabbitMQ must be reachable at
#      RABBITMQ_URL — the platform `logistics-rabbitmq` (dev/dev creds) is
#      likely already running (`docker ps`); set
#      RABBITMQ_URL=amqp://dev:dev@localhost:5672.
#
#   2. User JWTs signed with JWT_SECRET. tracking VERIFIES the inbound token
#      with JWT_SECRET (= auth-service's AUTH_JWT_SECRET); it does NOT mint
#      tokens. It needs `sub` + `role` (HS256). Only the owning customer, the
#      assigned driver, or an admin may read. Self-mint:
#        # a CUSTOMER token — sub MUST equal the order's customerId
#        node -e 'const jwt=require("jsonwebtoken"); console.log(jwt.sign({sub:"47913fd3-7bf9-4182-9d94-6144ddb74cfe", role:"customer"}, process.env.JWT_SECRET, {algorithm:"HS256", expiresIn:"30m"}))'
#        # an ADMIN token
#        node -e 'const jwt=require("jsonwebtoken"); console.log(jwt.sign({sub:"05950000-0000-7000-8000-00000000adm1", role:"admin"}, process.env.JWT_SECRET, {algorithm:"HS256", expiresIn:"30m"}))'
#      Run from this repo so jsonwebtoken + JWT_SECRET resolve, e.g.
#        export $(grep -v '^#' .env | xargs) && node -e '...'
#
# Usage:
#   1. Drive the projection + at least one point in (manual-testing-guide §4–§5).
#   2. Paste a customer/admin JWT into @token and set @orderId.
#   3. Click "Send Request".

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3005
@orderId = 06950000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a001

# Paste a valid user JWT — the owning customer (sub = the order's customerId),
# the assigned driver (sub = the driverId), or an admin (see prereq #2).
@token = <paste a CUSTOMER/ADMIN JWT>


############################################################
# Health
############################################################

### healthz — liveness (always 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz

### readyz — readiness (200 when Mongo + RabbitMQ channel + Redis are healthy)
GET {{baseUrl}}/readyz


############################################################
# REST reads (owning customer / assigned driver / admin only)
############################################################

### Latest known point for the order → 200 { orderId, lat, lng, ts } (404 if no point yet)
# (Same path direct or via the gateway: GET /v1/tracking/orders/{id}/latest.)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tracking/orders/{{orderId}}/latest
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Full ordered route for the order → 200 { orderId, points: [{ lat, lng, ts }, ...] }
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tracking/orders/{{orderId}}/route
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


############################################################
# Negative-path probes (intentionally fail; for spot-checking error shapes)
############################################################

### No auth — expect 401 unauthorized
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tracking/orders/{{orderId}}/latest

### Bogus JWT — expect 401 unauthorized
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tracking/orders/{{orderId}}/latest
Authorization: Bearer not.a.real.jwt

### Read another customer's order (sub != the order's customerId, role customer) — expect 404 (existence hidden; same as an unknown order)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tracking/orders/{{orderId}}/latest
Authorization: Bearer <paste a DIFFERENT customer's JWT>

### Read a nonexistent / not-yet-tracked order (admin) — expect 404 not_found
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tracking/orders/06950000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ffff/latest
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
